{"name":"Elegant Silk","hex":"#217f74","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elegant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterised by or exhibiting elegance; having grace, refinement, or tasteful simplicity.","Characterised by minimalism and intuitiveness while preserving exactness and precision."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elegant parrot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elegant"},{"term":"silk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fine fiber excreted by the silkworm or other arthropod (such as a spider).","A thread or yarn made from silk fibers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To develop silk.","To remove the silk from (corn)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elegance","blocks":[{"text":"Elegance is beauty that shows unusual effectiveness and simplicity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Pythagorean_proof_%281%29.svg/330px-Pythagorean_proof_%281%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elegance"},{"title":"Silk","blocks":[{"text":"Silk is a natural protein fiber, some forms of which can be woven or knitted into textiles. The protein fiber of silk is composed mainly of fibroin (75-80%) and a smaller coating of sericin (20-25%). It is most commonly produced from the cocoons of certain insect larvae. The best-known silk is obtained from the cocoons of the larvae of the mulberry silkworm Bombyx mori, which are reared in captivity (sericulture)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Silk_raw_01a.jpg/330px-Silk_raw_01a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silk"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Soulacroix_-_Elegance_Of_The_Epoque.jpg/500px-Fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_Soulacroix_-_